  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para dir="ltr">The scatter plot below shows the age (in years) and the price (in dollars) of used compact cars advertised in the local newspaper.</para>
<para dir="ltr"><figure><media alt="A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS AGE IN YEARS ON THE X-AXIS AND PRICE IN DOLLARS ON THE Y-AXIS. THE LINE DRAWN DECREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT AND PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (13, 6000) AND (7, 12000)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5f33547a78f8e26377fee2ffa0e7817c8d39546a"/></media></figure></para>
<para dir="ltr">Nora drew a line to fit the data. What is the slope of her line, and what does it mean in the problem?</para></section>
</content>
